# Forms — React Hook Form + Zod + shadcn

## Schema First

Always define the Zod schema before writing the form. Place schemas in `src/features/<feature>/schemas/`.
Derive the TypeScript type from the schema — never write types manually.

```typescript
// src/features/auth/schemas/auth.schema.ts
import { z } from "zod";

export const loginSchema = z.object({
  email: z.string().email("Invalid email address"),
  password: z.string().min(8, "Password must be at least 8 characters"),
});

export const registerSchema = z
  .object({
    firstName: z.string().min(2, "First name must be at least 2 characters"),
    lastName: z.string().min(2, "Last name must be at least 2 characters"),
    email: z.string().email("Invalid email address"),
    password: z.string().min(8, "Password must be at least 8 characters"),
    confirmPassword: z.string(),
  })
  .refine((data) => data.password === data.confirmPassword, {
    message: "Passwords do not match",
    path: ["confirmPassword"],
  });

// Always derive types from schemas — never write manually
export type LoginFields = z.infer<typeof loginSchema>;
export type RegisterFields = z.infer<typeof registerSchema>;
```

